1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:04,171
OKAY, RACH, THAT'S MUFFIN
AND ESPRESSO, $4.50

2
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:05,840
ROSS, DOUBLE LATTE, $2.75

3
00:00:05,881 --> 00:00:08,759
CHANDLER, COFFEE
AND SCONE, $4.25

4
00:00:08,801 --> 00:00:10,594
AND PHEEBS, HERBAL TEA, $1.25.

5
00:00:10,636 --> 00:00:13,597
SO, ALL TOGETHER, THAT'S $12.75.

6
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:15,140
THIS COMING FROM THE MAN

7
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:17,225
WHO COULDN'T SPLIT
OUR $80 PHONE BILL IN HALF.

8
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:19,603
HI.
HI.

9
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:21,689
HOW MUCH DO I OWE
FOR THE MUFFIN AND LATTE?

10
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,440
THAT'S ON THE HOUSE

11
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:25,108
COURTESY OF
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

12
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,568
OH, GREAT.

13
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:27,987
WELL, TELL HIM THANKS.

14
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:31,072
AND SINCE, UH, JOEY
SEEMS LIKE SUCH A NICE GUY

15
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:33,283
MAYBE WE COULD
GO ON A DATE SOMETIME.

16
00:00:33,325 --> 00:00:35,911
WELL, HE'S NOT USED
TO WOMEN BEING SO FORWARD

17
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:37,830
BUT, UH, I COULD
CHECK WITH HIM.

18
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:39,164
HE SAYS IT'S OKAY.

19
00:00:41,208 --> 00:00:43,293
GREAT. THANKS.
BYE-BYE.

20
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:45,796
HEY, JOEY, HOW COME
OUR STUFF ISN'T FREE?

21
00:00:45,838 --> 00:00:48,047
IT WILL BE WHEN YOU
LOOK LIKE THAT

22
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,633
IN A TIGHT SKIRT.

23
00:00:49,675 --> 00:00:51,802
THIS IS GREAT. I'M GETTING
MORE DATES THAT EVER.

24
00:00:51,844 --> 00:00:53,554
WAIT A MINUTE.

25
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:56,015
JOEY, YOU'RE ONLY
GIVING AWAY FREE STUFF
TO THE PRETTY GIRLS?

26
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,391
JOEY, THAT IS
SO GROSS.

27
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:00,227
HOW ABOUT A SCONE
ON THE HOUSE, BABY?

28
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:03,397
I'M PRETTY.

29
00:01:10,529 --> 00:01:15,910
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

30
00:01:15,951 --> 00:01:18,161
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

31
00:01:18,203 --> 00:01:20,414
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

32
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:25,419
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

33
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,671
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

34
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:31,008
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

35
00:01:31,050 --> 00:01:34,219
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

36
00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:40,141
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO... ♪

37
00:01:44,772 --> 00:01:46,189
HEY, DOES ANYONE
HAVE ANY GUM?

38
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,232
OH, I DO.

39
00:01:49,735 --> 00:01:51,820
HERE, SORRY.

40
00:01:51,862 --> 00:01:54,949
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

41
00:01:57,076 --> 00:01:58,702
NO.

42
00:01:59,912 --> 00:02:01,789
WAIT A SECOND...

43
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:05,208
( plastic bag rustling )

44
00:02:08,127 --> 00:02:09,671
I KNOW IT'S IN
HERE SOMEWHERE.

45
00:02:09,713 --> 00:02:11,548
YOU KNOW WHAT,
I'M GOOD, I'M GOOD.

46
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:12,591
HEY.

47
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:13,842
HEY, WHAT ARE
YOU DOING HERE?

48
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:15,052
SHOULDN'T YOU BE AT WORK?

49
00:02:15,094 --> 00:02:16,386
UH, THEY SENT ME HOME.

50
00:02:16,428 --> 00:02:18,472
THEY SAID I CAN'T WORK
IF I'M SICK.

51
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:19,765
All:
OH!

52
00:02:19,807 --> 00:02:20,849
I'M SORRY YOU'RE SICK.

53
00:02:20,891 --> 00:02:21,976
I'M NOT SICK!

54
00:02:23,769 --> 00:02:24,812
I DON'T GET SICK.

55
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,605
GETTING SICK IS FOR WEAKLINGS.

56
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:28,482
IT'S FOR PANSIES.

57
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:31,026
HONEY, NO ONE THINKS
THAT YOU'RE A PANSY.

58
00:02:31,068 --> 00:02:34,696
BUT WE DO THINK
THAT YOU NEED A TISSUE.

59
00:02:36,949 --> 00:02:39,660
I HAVE NOT BEEN SICK
IN OVER THREE YEARS.

60
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:41,036
( sneezes )

61
00:02:41,078 --> 00:02:42,830
I'M GOING TO GRAB YOU
SOME TISSUE.

62
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:44,498
I-I DON'T NEED

63
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:45,582
A TISSUE!

64
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:46,959
I'M FINE'D!

65
00:02:47,001 --> 00:02:49,461
WHEN YOU PUT A "D"
AT THE END OF "FINE"

66
00:02:49,503 --> 00:02:52,089
YOU'RE NOT FINE.

67
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:55,634
I'M FINE... 'D.

68
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,136
I'M FINE... 'D.

69
00:02:57,176 --> 00:02:58,386
OKAY.

70
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:00,931
YOU KNOW, IT'S
A REALLY HARD WORD TO SAY.

71
00:03:00,973 --> 00:03:02,265
( knocking on door )

72
00:03:14,069 --> 00:03:15,029
YES?

73
00:03:15,070 --> 00:03:16,195
HI. IS RACHEL HERE?

74
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:17,364
I'M HER SISTER.

75
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:18,824
OH, MY GOD! JILL!

76
00:03:18,866 --> 00:03:20,199
OH, MY GOD! RACHEL!

77
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:21,702
HI!

78
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:22,744
OH, MY GOD!

79
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:24,038
INTRODUCE US.

80
00:03:24,079 --> 00:03:26,165
WELL, THIS IS CHANDLER.

81
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,708
AND YOU KNOW
MONICA AND ROSS.

82
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,126
AND THAT'S PHOEBE

83
00:03:29,168 --> 00:03:30,209
AND THAT'S JOEY.

84
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:31,545
HEY, HOW YOU DOING?

85
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:32,253
DON'T!

86
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:39,720
HONEY, WHAT ARE
YOU DOING HERE?

87
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:41,346
WHICH-WHICH
SISTER IS THIS?

88
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:44,265
IS THIS THE SPOILED ONE
OR THE ONE THAT BIT HER?

89
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,767
DADDY CUT ME OFF.

90
00:03:45,809 --> 00:03:47,895
NEVER MIND. I GOT IT.

91
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,354
AND YOU KNOW
WHAT I SAID TO HIM?

92
00:03:49,396 --> 00:03:50,981
I SAID, "I'M GOING
TO HIRE A LAWYER

93
00:03:51,023 --> 00:03:52,107
"AND I'M GOING
TO SUE YOU

94
00:03:52,149 --> 00:03:53,567
"AND TAKE
ALL YOUR MONEY

95
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,860
AND THEN I'M GOING
TO CUT YOU OFF!"

96
00:03:54,902 --> 00:03:56,570
WOW, WHAT DID HE SAY?

97
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:58,530
HE SAID HE WOULDN'T
PAY FOR MY LAWYER.

98
00:03:58,572 --> 00:04:01,950
AND THEN HE TOLD ME
TO COME HERE AND LEARN
ABOUT THE VALUE OF MONEY

99
00:04:01,992 --> 00:04:04,244
FROM THE ONE
DAUGHTER HE'S
ACTUALLY PROUD OF.

100
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:05,913
( gasps )

101
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:07,330
DID YOU HEAR THAT?

102
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,999
MY DAD'S PROUD OF ME.

103
00:04:09,041 --> 00:04:11,543
MY DAD'S PROUD OF ME.

104
00:04:11,585 --> 00:04:12,711
RACH...

105
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:13,754
OH, YEAH, SORRY.

106
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:15,672
OKAY, HONEY,
SO WHAT DID YOU DO

107
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:17,632
THAT MADE DAD
CUT YOU OFF?

108
00:04:17,674 --> 00:04:20,094
OKAY, I BOUGHT A BOAT.

109
00:04:20,135 --> 00:04:21,762
YOU BOUGHT A BOAT?

110
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:24,514
YEAH, BUT IT WASN'T FOR ME,
IT WAS FOR A FRIEND.

111
00:04:24,556 --> 00:04:28,309
BOY, DID WE MAKE FRIENDS
WITH THE WRONG SISTER.

112
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,606
JILL, HONEY,
I THINK THIS IS
THE BEST THING

113
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:34,482
THAT COULD HAVE
EVER HAPPENED TO YOU.

114
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:37,152
YOU'VE NEEDED TO GET OUT
ON YOUR OWN, ANYWAY.

115
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:38,612
AND, YOU KNOW,
WHEN I DID IT

116
00:04:38,653 --> 00:04:39,947
I-I, AT FIRST
I WAS SCARED,

117
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:41,240
BUT THEN,
LOOK AT ME NOW.

118
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:42,323
I AM THE
ONLY DAUGHTER

119
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:44,034
THAT DAD IS PROUD OF.

120
00:04:44,076 --> 00:04:45,786
OKAY, THIS
IS WHAT

121
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:46,787
YOU'RE GOING TO DO.

122
00:04:46,828 --> 00:04:48,247
YOU'RE GOING
TO GET A JOB.

123
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,998
YOU'RE GOING
TO GET AN APARTMENT.

124
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:51,166
AND THEN
I'LL HELP YOU

125
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:52,876
AND YOU CAN
STAY WITH US.

126
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:53,961
RIGHT, PHEEBS?

127
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,629
OF COURSE, YEAH.

128
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:56,797
OH, THAT'S SO GREAT.

129
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:58,632
OKAY, I'M REALLY
GOING TO DO THIS.

130
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:00,592
I DON'T KNOW HOW
TO THANK YOU GUYS.

131
00:05:00,634 --> 00:05:03,011
OH, I LIKE CARS.

132
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:11,145
UH, ARE YOU
ALL FINISHED HERE?
YES.

133
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:13,063
GREAT.

134
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:17,609
OKAY, HERE ARE
THE TIPS FOR
THIS MORNING.

135
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:18,652
MM.

136
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:20,195
JAN GETS $50, $50 FOR ME

137
00:05:20,237 --> 00:05:22,948
AND JOEY OWES
EIGHT DOLLARS.

138
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:24,908
WHAT?

139
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:26,701
FOR ALL THE FREE FOOD
YOU GAVE AWAY.

140
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:28,036
WELL, IF IT'S
FREE FOOD

141
00:05:28,078 --> 00:05:29,788
HOW COME YOU'RE
CHARGING ME FOR IT?

142
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,581
WE DON'T GIVE
ANYTHING AWAY

143
00:05:31,623 --> 00:05:33,917
UNLESS IT'S
SOMEONE'S BIRTHDAY.

144
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:37,712
OH... WHA-WHAT IF
THEY CAME IN THIRD
IN A MODELING CONTEST?

145
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,089
NO.

146
00:05:39,131 --> 00:05:40,090
HMM...

147
00:05:40,132 --> 00:05:42,050
SORRY.

148
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:46,721
I JUST HAD THE HARDEST DAY.

149
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:48,807
SOME OF THESE ARE SO HEAVY.

150
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:50,725
JILL, HOW DID YOU PAY
FOR ALL THIS?

151
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:53,312
I THOUGHT YOUR DAD
TOOK AWAY YOUR CREDIT CARD.

152
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:56,148
OH, PLEASE. I MEMORIZED
THOSE NUMBERS WHEN I WAS 15.

153
00:05:57,356 --> 00:06:00,610
BUT, LOOK AT ALL THE COOL
MAKE-IT-ON-MY-OWN STUFF I GOT.

154
00:06:00,652 --> 00:06:03,113
THIS IS
MY "PLEASE HIRE ME" SWEATER.

155
00:06:03,155 --> 00:06:04,948
AND THESE ARE MY...

156
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:07,993
"DON'T YOU WANT TO RENT ME
THIS APARTMENT?" PANTS.

157
00:06:08,035 --> 00:06:11,038
I DON'T THINK CHARGING
NEW CLOTHES TO YOUR DAD

158
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:13,832
QUALIFIES AS MAKING IT
ON YOUR OWN.

159
00:06:13,874 --> 00:06:16,375
OH, MR. SCIENTIST
HAS TO GET ALL TECHNICAL.

160
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:20,714
SERIOUSLY, I DON'T THINK
RACHEL'S GOING TO THINK
IT'S SUCH A GOOD IDEA.

161
00:06:20,755 --> 00:06:22,423
SO, WHO MADE HER
QUEEN OF THE WORLD?

162
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,467
OH, I WOULD
LOVE THAT JOB.

163
00:06:25,593 --> 00:06:27,554
HEY, WHAT'S GOING ON?

164
00:06:27,595 --> 00:06:28,638
HEY.

165
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:29,723
JILL...

166
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:33,018
DID YOU SHOP?

167
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,435
NO.

168
00:06:34,477 --> 00:06:36,688
THEY DID.

169
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:39,983
Both:
YEAH, WE WENT SHOPPING!

170
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:43,028
YOU WENT SHOPPING?

171
00:06:43,070 --> 00:06:44,696
WHAT? AND THEN YOU
JUST CAME IN HERE

172
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:46,781
AND PARADED IT
RIGHT UNDER JILL'S NOSE

173
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,700
WHEN YOU KNOW
SHE'S TRYING TO QUIT?

174
00:06:48,742 --> 00:06:50,369
WOW, YOU GUYS, IT'S TERRIBLE.

175
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:51,536
SORRY, JILL.

176
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:52,871
SORRY-SORRY, JILL.

177
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:54,956
SO, WHAT

178
00:06:54,998 --> 00:06:55,832
DID YOU GET?

179
00:06:55,874 --> 00:06:57,376
OH, WELL,
ALL RIGHT

180
00:06:57,416 --> 00:07:01,755
I GOT... THANK YOU, I GOT THIS
"I WANT A JOB" SWEATER.

181
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:02,964
OH.

182
00:07:03,006 --> 00:07:05,967
AND THEN I GOT,
UH, THESE...

183
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:08,511
ARE APARTMENT
PANTS.

184
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:12,307
APARTMENT PANTS?

185
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:15,227
YEAH, YOU'VE NEVER
HEARD OF THEM?

186
00:07:15,269 --> 00:07:18,230
WELL, NO, OF COURSE,
OF COURSE I'VE HEARD OF THEM.

187
00:07:18,272 --> 00:07:20,481
ROSS, WHAT
DID YOU GET?

188
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:21,566
HUH?

189
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:26,280
I GOT THIS... THIS.

190
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:29,574
A PASHMINA?

191
00:07:29,616 --> 00:07:31,701
YEAH.

192
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:35,705
I-I LOVE THESE BABIES.

193
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:39,960
REALLY?

194
00:07:40,001 --> 00:07:41,044
MM.

195
00:07:41,086 --> 00:07:42,545
ROSS, WHAT'S A PASHMINA?

196
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:44,923
IT'S A RUG.

197
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:48,260
JILL.

198
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:50,262
( fake crying and sobbing )

199
00:07:50,304 --> 00:07:52,597
I'M SORRY, RACHEL.

200
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:54,099
OH, COME ON.

201
00:07:54,141 --> 00:07:56,393
YOU REALLY THINK
THAT'S GOING TO WORK ON ME?

202
00:07:56,435 --> 00:07:57,644
I INVENTED THAT.

203
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:58,812
RIGHT.

204
00:07:58,853 --> 00:08:00,981
BUT I AM SORRY.

205
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,232
ALL RIGHT, IT'S OKAY.

206
00:08:02,274 --> 00:08:03,317
ONE LITTLE SETBACK

207
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:04,859
IS OKAY.

208
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,903
BUT JUST DON'T LET IT
HAPPEN AGAIN, ALL RIGHT?

209
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:08,238
OKAY.

210
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:10,073
NOW, SINCE DADDY
PAID FOR ALL
THIS STUFF

211
00:08:10,115 --> 00:08:11,950
I SHOULD TAKE IT ALL AWAY

212
00:08:11,992 --> 00:08:14,661
BUT I'M JUST GOING TO TAKE...

213
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:16,246
THE-THE PASHMINA.

214
00:08:18,332 --> 00:08:20,000
AND THE-AND THE, UH, PANTS.

215
00:08:20,041 --> 00:08:22,294
AND, YOU KNOW WHAT, I'M JUST
GOING TO TAKE IT ALL AWAY

216
00:08:22,336 --> 00:08:25,213
'CAUSE THAT WAY, YOU'LL JUST
REALLY LEARN THE LESSON, OKAY?

217
00:08:25,255 --> 00:08:26,256
ALL RIGHTY.

218
00:08:26,298 --> 00:08:27,382
WELL, I'M GOING

219
00:08:27,424 --> 00:08:28,800
TO RUN A COUPLE OF ERRANDS

220
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,385
AND I WILL SEE YOU AT DINNER.

221
00:08:31,552 --> 00:08:33,930
( sighs )

222
00:08:33,972 --> 00:08:36,599
SHE TOOK ALL
MY STUFF.

223
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:38,935
YEAH, EVERYTHING BUT...

224
00:08:38,977 --> 00:08:40,645
THE LITTLE BLUE ONE.

225
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:41,729
( gasps )

226
00:08:41,771 --> 00:08:43,190
OH! THAT'S
THE BEST ONE!

227
00:08:43,231 --> 00:08:45,733
OH, MY GOD!
THANK YOU SO MUCH!

228
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,152
WELL, HEY...

229
00:08:47,194 --> 00:08:50,322
OH, MY GOSH,
THAT WAS SO LAME.

230
00:08:50,364 --> 00:08:52,115
LIKE A PASHMINA
COULD BE A RUG.

231
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:54,159
OH, YEAH, WELL,
HOW ABOUT YOU WITH

232
00:08:54,201 --> 00:08:55,994
"OH, I'M SORRY..."

233
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:57,954
OH, SHUT UP! IT
WASN'T LIKE
THAT AT ALL.

234
00:08:57,996 --> 00:09:00,040
WHAT ABOUT- WHAT ABOUT
WHAT I SAID

235
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:01,666
ABOUT THE APARTMENT PANTS?

236
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,043
HOW DUMB WAS I? HA!

237
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,588
WERE YOU THIS CUTE
IN HIGH SCHOOL?

238
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,174
OH, STOP.

239
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:10,425
NO, YOU STOP.

240
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:11,426
NO, YOU STOP.

241
00:09:11,468 --> 00:09:12,593
YOU STOP.

242
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:13,928
OKAY, OKAY,
WHY DON'T
I SIT HERE

243
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:15,389
AND THEN YOU'LL
BOTH STOP IT.

244
00:09:18,599 --> 00:09:20,727
OKAY, SO WHAT
DO YOU WANT TO DO?

245
